lisptc

A Lisp interpreter designed to be the deterministic "brain" of an AI agent in
a neuro-symbolic architecture. The LLM writes Lisp code into a REPL; the
REPL's state and output steer the LLM's context back. Two sides of one
system:

- the LLM: creative, inspired, encodes tacit knowledge
- the Lisp runtime: logical, deterministic, experience-driven, holds memory

They both write to each other.

Write-up: https://d4shi.com/blog/lisptc/

SHAPE

The interpreter is the core dialect and nothing else. Every surface past it
lives in an extension, and an extension is one language surface plus the
prompt that teaches it.

Three rules hold the thing together, and CI fails on each of them:

- Dependencies run one way: interpreter, extensions, REPL front-ends, agent,
  apps.
- Everything an extension does that reaches outside the process goes through
  a port it declares itself. It never picks where a server runs, where a
  token is written, or which model answers.
- Nothing above an extension names it. Behaviour crosses the seam as a chain
  an extension hooks, a capability as a slot it fills, data as an annotation
  it attaches. Extensions are named at a composition root, and there are only
  two.

Every workspace carries an AGENTS.md with the rules that govern it. That is
the entry point for working in one. The code carries no comments and there
are no design docs: a constraint worth keeping is a name, a type, or a test.

REPO LAYOUT (pnpm + Turborepo monorepo)

The language

  packages/interpreter    @repo/interpreter. The reader, the evaluator, the
                          drivers, the prelude, and the three seam mechanisms
                          an extension plugs into. Ships no extension and
                          names none.

The extensions, one language surface each

  packages/compaction     @repo/compaction-extension. Bounded output, so a
                          large result never floods the context.
  packages/llm            @repo/llm-extension. The language model as a
                          callable value.
  packages/mcp            @repo/mcp-extension. MCP servers, their tools, and
                          the OAuth to reach the remote ones.
  packages/memory         @repo/memory-extension. What the agent keeps and
                          recalls across sessions.
  packages/promises       @repo/promises-extension. Asynchrony over a
                          synchronous evaluator.
  packages/prose          @repo/prose-extension. The prose the model writes
                          around its forms.
  packages/secrets        @repo/secrets-extension. The secret registry, with
                          taint-tracked redaction.
  packages/ui-extension   @repo/ui-extension. Widgets the agent renders to a
                          client.
  packages/checks         @repo/checks. The DSL an eval case is written in.

Everything else

  packages/repl           @repo/repl. REPL front-ends over the interpreter:
                          an embeddable string-in/string-out REPL, and a
                          shared-session server over a unix socket so an
                          editor's LSP and a terminal REPL share one
                          interpreter.
  packages/ai             @repo/ai. The agent loop and what it runs on.
  packages/evals          @repo/evals. The eval driver, the report it writes,
                          and everything that reads one back.
  packages/backend        @repo/backend. The Convex deployment, and the Better
                          Auth instance whose database is Convex itself.
  packages/env            @repo/env. Typed env. The only place process.env is
                          read.
  packages/shared         @repo/shared. The no-dependency utility layer.
  packages/syntax         @repo/syntax. The lisptc language for the
                          highlighter.
  packages/ui             @repo/ui. The base design system.
  packages/components     @repo/components. The components we wrote, on top of
                          @repo/ui.
  packages/bloub          @repo/bloub. The avatar component and its engine.
  packages/tsconfigs      Shared tsconfig bases.

Apps

  apps/api                An HTTP server streaming the agent loop.
  apps/app                The web frontend.
  apps/cli                @lisptc/cli. The interactive terminal REPL, shipped
                          as the lisptc binary: it runs .ptc files, drops into
                          a prompt, or attaches to the shared session server
                          instead of a local interpreter.
  apps/lsp                @lisptc/lsp. A stdio language server: diagnostics
                          from static syntax and arity checking, plus
                          completion and hover against a live shared session.
  apps/mcp                @lisptc/mcp-repl. A stdio MCP server exposing the
                          REPL itself as an MCP tool.
  apps/mcp-toolkit        @lisptc/mcp-toolkit. The MCP servers we write
                          ourselves, pointing outward.
  apps/trace-viewer       @lisptc/trace-viewer. A viewer for eval runs, and
                          the home of the eval cases and their concrete hosts.

Outside the workspaces

  editors/nvim            A Neovim plugin: filetype detection, LSP client
                          wiring, and a REPL client against the shared
                          session.
  tree-sitter-lisptc      The tree-sitter grammar for the dialect.
  examples/               Runnable .ptc walkthroughs: basics, control flow,
                          macros and functions, json, memory, secrets, and
                          MCP including Linear and Playwright.
  scripts/                The architecture, comment, docs and reference checks
                          CI runs.

THE LANGUAGE

Core dialect:

- reader, evaluator, tail-call optimisation, closures, macros
- quote, quasiquote, unquote and unquote-splicing
- try/catch and error
- a module system: (import "path") with cycle detection
- docstrings on defun and defmacro, doc coverage for every global binding
- a prelude in Lisp: lists and alists, strings and format, let, let*, letrec,
  cond, when, unless, while, dolist, dotimes, case, mapcar, filter, reduce

What the extensions add on top:

- compaction   echo, doc, head, tail, grep
- promises     await, promise-all, promise-all-settled, promise-any,
               promise-race, promise-state, promises, cancel
- llm          llm/complete, llm/chat, llm/extract, llm/providers, message,
               and the shape macros that type an extraction
- mcp          load-mcp, unload-mcp, list-mcps, search-mcps, list-tools,
               search-tools, login, logout, mcp-authorize, mcp-shutdown.
               A loaded tool becomes a callable binding (server/tool), and
               loading never blocks: the work runs off an async broker and
               applies between evaluations.
- memory       memory/remember, memory/recall, memory/revise, memory/forget,
               memory/replay, memories
- secrets      secrets and secret, returning tainted strings the string
               builtins carry through and the printer redacts
- ui           ui/text, ui/heading, ui/markdown, ui/link, ui/badge, ui/kpi,
               ui/stack, ui/row, ui/card, ui/button, ui/input, ui/select,
               ui/checkbox, ui/form, ui/table, ui/send, ui/render
- prose        no new bindings. It lets the model write prose around its
               forms.
- checks       the eval DSL: called, awaited, answered, errored, halted,
               matches, contains, eventually, never, always, before, after,
               within, once, at-most

COMMANDS

  pnpm test              vitest in each package
  pnpm typecheck         tsc --noEmit per package
  pnpm lint              biome ci (matches CI)
  pnpm format            biome check --write
  pnpm knip              dead code and unused dependencies
  pnpm boundaries        package layering and import rules
  pnpm check:arch        the manifest rules boundaries cannot express
  pnpm check:comments    fails on any non-directive comment
  pnpm check:docs        fails on tracked markdown outside the allowlist
  pnpm check:refs        AGENTS.md references that no longer resolve
  pnpm repl              run the REPL against a local interpreter
  pnpm repl:attach       attach to (or spawn) the shared session server
  pnpm test:evals        the agent evals, against real models
  pnpm test:nvim         the Neovim integration test

  task up                build and run the whole stack in docker, live reload
  task down              stop it (pass -- -v to drop its data)
  task evals:run         run the eval suite
  task evals:open        build the trace viewer, serve it, open a browser
  task test              pnpm tests, nix flake checks, and the nvim test
  task check:agents      judge the AGENTS.md prose a PR adds

A task that needs credentials runs under Infisical, so they reach the command
without ever landing in a file.

Requires Node >= 22.6.0 and pnpm 10.28.0. .ts files run directly through
Node's type stripping, with no build step.
